A||N||2||Rhpetterson||Power Door Locks!?||||1||
Z||000000||Rhpetterson||03-11-2001||02:32 PM||||when i push the power door lock button nothing happens just a clicking noise coming from under the dash. if i repeatedly push the button the locks will jump sometimes. Anyone know the problem???????????||||reg||1
Z||000001||Lisa 86 2m4||03-11-2001||05:01 PM||||My guess is that your lock cylinders have rusted and refuse to budge. Can you lock/unlock manually? Easily?  IF not, then it's time to change the lock cylinders. I just did all of that about 1 month ago for the same reason.<BR>Lisa||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||03-11-2001||09:18 PM||||Could also be as simple as bad/corroded connections from the door wiring harness to the lock solenoid.  Remove the door panel, and remove the connector from the solenoid.  There is a little tab that you squeeze while you pull it out.  Clean both sides of each connection with steel wool or sand paper to scuff it up, and them some electronics cleaner.  If that dosent do it, just keep backtracking the wires from there.<P>The clicking you hear is the relay, which is located under the passenger side dash speaker, bolted to the frame.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
